 "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hello!\r\n\r\nI'm not sure if this is an IDE specific problem or not. I am new to this. Please forgive me.\r\n\r\nI'm using the prebuild mavsdk-windows-x64-release.zip from [1.4.6] on Windows 10 .0.1945.\r\nI extracted the zip to a local folder \"C:\\SharedLibs\\mavsdk_superbuild\".\r\nI tried the takeoff_and_land example from the 1.4.6 tree.\r\nI'm using the VS 2019 Version 16.10.4 IDE and set the project properties (Release/x64) as follows:\r\n\r\nC/C++: Additional Include Directories: C:\\SharedLibs\\mavsdk_superbuild\\include\r\nC/C++: C++ Language Standard: ISO C++17 Standard (/std:c++17)\r\nLinker: Additional Library Directories: C:\\SharedLibs\\mavsdk_superbuild\\lib\r\nLinker: Additional Dependencies: mavsdk.lib\r\n\r\nBuilding the example in the IDE (Release/x64) throws me:\r\n\r\n>Build started...\r\n1>------ Build started: Project: takeoff_and_land, Configuration: Release x64 ------\r\n1>mavsdk.lib(system_impl.obj) : error LNK2001: unresolved external symbol __std_find_trivial_8\r\n1>C:\\Users\\Chris\\source\\repos\\takeoff_and_land\\x64\\Release\\takeoff_and_land.exe : fatal error LNK1120: 1 unresolved externals\r\n1>Done building project \"takeoff_and_land.vcxproj\" -- FAILED.\r\n========== Build: 0 succeeded, 1 failed, 0 up-to-date, 0 skipped ==========\r\n<\r\n\r\nObviously the linker isn't happy. What am I doing wrong?\r\n\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "JonasVautherin", "id": 2606672, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI2MDY2NzI=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2606672?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin", "html_url": "https://github.com/JonasVautherin", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/JonasVautherin/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/Jona